f commercial vehicle attachments and equipment in North America. It operates in two segments, Work Truck Attachments and Work Truck Solutions. The Work Truck Attachments segment manufactures and sells snow and ice control attachments, and other products sold under the FISHER, WESTERN, and SNOWEX brands, as well as truck-mounted service cranes and dump hoists under the VENCO and VENTURO brands. The Work Truck Solutions segment engages in the manufacturing of municipal snow and ice control products under the HENDERSON brand; and upfit of attachments and storage under the HENDERSON and DEJANA brands, and related sub brands. The company also provides customized turnkey solutions to governmental agencies, such as departments of transportation and municipalities. It sells its products through a distributor network primarily to professional snowplowers who are contracted to remove snow and ice from commercial and residential areas. Douglas Dynamics, Inc. was founded in 1946 and is headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark Van Genderen | President, CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $372K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $36K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Douglas Dynamics, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $864M market cap on $656M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 30%.","The business throws off $64M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.59\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield of 3.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 22% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Douglas Dynamics Inc. (PLOW) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/How_Douglas_Dynamics_Inc._PLOW_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_111326021201_1794553921.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794553921.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Comparing Gates Industrial (NYSE:GTES) & Douglas Dynamics (NYSE:PLOW)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/comparing-gates-industrial-nysegtes-douglas-dynamics-nyseplow.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794079016.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.945,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Western Products Auctions One-of-a-Kind Pusher Plow Honoring America's 250th Anniversary to Support Camp Hometown Heroes","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/small-business/articles/western-products-auctions-one-kind-014000185.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793929200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.912,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Douglas Dynamics (NYSE:PLOW) Issues FY 2026 Earnings Guidance","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/douglas-dynamics-nyseplow-issues-fy-2026-earnings-guidance.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793880711.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.827,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance","legal"]},{"title":"Douglas Dynamics Inc (PLOW) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Sales, Raised Guidance, ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/douglas-dynamics-inc-plow-q3-010651384.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793754411.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Douglas Dynamics (PLOW) Stock Drops As Q3 Earnings Meet Cash Flo